      "text": "HISTORY AND PHYSICAL\n\nPatient: Larsen-Hughes, Colleen\nMRN: 6167853    Account: ACCT1068456722\nDOB: 1980-08-17    Date of admission: 2025-04-11\nAttending: Dr. Nash\nPCP: Mei Long, PA-C\nInsurance ID: DWJ194963587\n\nCHIEF COMPLAINT: cough and fever.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS:\nMrs. Larsen-Hughes is a 44-year-old woman with a history of asthma, hypertension, former tobacco use who presents with cough and fever. She reports five days of productive cough, fevers to 101.8 F, and pleuritic chest pain on the right.\n\nPAST MEDICAL HISTORY: asthma, hypertension, former tobacco use. Prior related evaluation on 2023-12-05.\nMEDICATIONS: amoxicillin-clavulanate 875/125 mg twice daily; albuterol inhaler as needed.\n\nSOCIAL HISTORY: Lives at 5338 Meadow Rd, Eastvale, IL 54219. Lives with Kenneth. Emergency contact is Harriet Larsen-Hughes, reachable at 681.555.0181. Patient's cell phone is 528.555.0137.\n\nOBJECTIVE: BP 120/66, HR 113, RR 14, Temp 99.9 F, SpO2 93%. Pain 7/10. Crackles and egophony at the right base. No accessory muscle use.\nLABS: WBC 14.2, procalcitonin 1.9, lactate 1.4.\nIMAGING: Right lower lobe airspace opacity consistent with pneumonia. No effusion.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN: community-acquired pneumonia (ICD-10 K35.80). Ceftriaxone 1 g daily and azithromycin 500 mg daily, supplemental oxygen to keep saturation above 92%.\nDiscussed with Dr. Sandoval (cardiology); Dr. Sandoval recommends outpatient follow-up with primary care.\nAdmitted to room 304.\n\nElectronically signed by Priya Larsen, NP on April 11, 2025."
